From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Madej <l.madej@grinn-global.com>
Date: Thu, 15 May 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] board: dolphin: disable rescue-mode GPIO trigger

The dolphin board late init unconditionally probes a jumper between
PortB6 (GPIO38) and PortB7 (GPIO39) to decide whether to enter rescue
mode. On grinn-astra-1680-sbc those pins are routed differently than
on the Synaptics reference board, so the detection falsely triggers
on every boot and forces the device into rescue mode.

Disable the GPIO-based trigger on grinn-astra-1680-sbc. Rescue mode is
still reachable from the U-Boot prompt via `run rescue_boot`.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz Madej <l.madej@grinn-global.com>
---
 board/synaptics/dolphin/dolphin_boardinit.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/board/synaptics/dolphin/dolphin_boardinit.c b/board/synaptics/dolphin/dolphin_boardinit.c
--- a/board/synaptics/dolphin/dolphin_boardinit.c
+++ b/board/synaptics/dolphin/dolphin_boardinit.c
@@ -456,7 +456,7 @@ int board_late_init(void)

 #ifdef CONFIG_SYNA_RESCUE_MODE
 	setup_rescue_mode_gpio();
-	rescue_trigger_detect();
+	/* rescue_trigger_detect(); */ /* disabled: false-trigger on grinn-astra-1680-sbc */
 #endif

 #ifdef CONFIG_SYNA_TZ_MR
--
2.43.0
